{"meta": {"limit": 1000, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 60}, "objects": [{"ascii": "Rich Salz", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "I first got involved with the IETF back when I worked at BBN; my first acknowledgement was in RFC 2616. Over time, I become more involved in the definition of standards, along with their development and deployment. I have been involved in the Newcomers's presentation for many years, and also the WG Chairs meeting. I was a NomCom chair.\r\n\r\nI wrote INN, the major Usenet/NNTP implementation. For a number of years, I was a member of the OpenSSL project. It was the dominant SSL/TLS implementation (it probably still is, even today).\r\n\r\nMost of my career has been on one side of Cambridge, Massachusetts (Alewife) or the other (Kendall Square). I joined Akamai toward the end of 2012. I focus on making things more secure and easier, and helping Akamai implement IETF standards more quickly.\r\n\r\nDiversity and representation are important.", "id": 18427, "name": "Rich Salz", "name_from_draft": "Rich Salz", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/rsalz.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/rsalz_aDJGpCt.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/18427/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:05:29Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Dan Wing", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "", "id": 100038, "name": "Dan Wing", "name_from_draft": "Dan Wing", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/dan-wing-RMgvm.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/dan-wing-RMgvm-th.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/100038/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:03:56Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Michael Richardson", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "Michael Richardson is an open source and open standards consultant.\r\nAn autodidact, he wrote mail transfer agents as a teenager, and in the\r\n1990s, found his calling designing and building embedded networking products,\r\nin the security sector.  Michael has built multiple IPsec systems, joining\r\nthe FreeS/WAN team in 2001, and founding Xelerance in 2003.\r\nSince 2008 Michael has worked in and chaired the IETF ROLL working group,\r\ndoing routing protocols for IoT mesh systems.  Michael has authored a number\r\nof IoT related RFCs including RFC8366 and RFC7416.\r\nMichael currently works on IoT security systems in the 6tisch, ANIMA\r\nand ACE WG, specializing in the problem of initial bootstrap trust.\r\n\r\nMichael received a B. Sc. Physics from Carleton University in 1996.\r\nORCID: https://orcid.org/my-orcid?orcid=0000-0002-0773-8388", "id": 102254, "name": "Michael Richardson", "name_from_draft": "Michael Richardson", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/mcr-2022-kneeling-headshot.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/mcr-2022-kneeling-headshot_X2oqNMr.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['they/them']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/102254/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:04:56Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Yaron Sheffer", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "", "id": 104278, "name": "Yaron Sheffer", "name_from_draft": "Yaron Sheffer", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/yaron-sheffer-m4vd7_cSHc6jj.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/yaron-sheffer-m4vd7_a6z0cCe.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/104278/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:04:12Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Scott Fluhrer", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "", "id": 104548, "name": "Scott Fluhrer", "name_from_draft": "Scott Fluhrer", "photo": null, "photo_thumb": null, "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/104548/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:12:00Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Hannes Tschofenig", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "Hannes Tschofenig contributes to global standards to make the Internet more secure. He has been active in the IETF for the past 20 years and contributed to more than 90 RFCs on security, privacy and various Internet protocols. Hannes co-chaired several IETF working groups, including SCITT, OAuth, ACE, KEYPROV, DIME, and ECRIT. From 2010 to 2014 Hannes was a member of the Internet Architecture Board (IAB), a committee of the IETF.", "id": 105857, "name": "Hannes Tschofenig", "name_from_draft": "Hannes Tschofenig", "photo": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/HannesTschofenig.jpg", "photo_thumb": "https://www.ietf.org/lib/dt/media/photo/HannesTschofenig_vJjOwWD.jpg", "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/105857/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:03:57Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Lijun Liao", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "", "id": 107999, "name": "Lijun Liao", "name_from_draft": "Lijun Liao", "photo": null, "photo_thumb": null, "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "['he/him']", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/107999/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:18:29Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Evangelos Haleplidis", "ascii_short": "", "biography": "", "id": 110017, "name": "Evangelos Haleplidis", "name_from_draft": "Evangelos Haleplidis", "photo": null, "photo_thumb": null, "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "[]", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/110017/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:18:36Z", "user": ""}, {"ascii": "Srinivasa Addepalli", "ascii_short": null, "biography": "", "id": 110846, "name": "Srinivasa Addepalli", "name_from_draft": "Srinivasa Addepalli", "photo": null, "photo_thumb": null, "plain": "", "pronouns_freetext": null, "pronouns_selectable": "[]", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/person/person/110846/", "time": "2012-02-26T08:19:27Z", "user": null}, {"ascii": "Tir